    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of seven consecutive integers is divisible by 7.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$7(n+3)$, so the sum is divisible by 7.\n\nRepresent the integers as $n,n+1,\\ldots,n+6$ and factor their sum.",
      "worked": "Let the integers be $n,n+1,\\ldots,n+6$, where $n$ is an integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n+(n+1)+\\cdots+(n+6)&=7n+21\\\\n+(n+1)+\\cdots+(n+6)&=7(n+3).\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $n+3$ is an integer, the sum is divisible by 7.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
